{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BNUB5pEvdotc1UDDPwAc4Z","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"schema_version\": 1,\n  \"canonical_task\": {\n    \"path\": \"task.md\",\n    \"sha256\": \"e4935f14c47be3f40dba4b1e04f0cc983f4d8d35b139befe19b98f5b4ec88e67\"\n  },\n  \"method\": {\n    \"class\": \"Evaluator-verified adversarial data-perturbation search (drop/flip edits, influence- or refit-guided) for Bradley-Terry pairwise-comparison leaderboard sensitivity\",\n    \"description\": \"A candidate receives anonymized comparison arrays (model_a, model_b, outcome) and a budget k (0.1%-2% of rows) and proposes at most k row indices to drop or flip so that the baseline rank-1 competitor loses rank 1. The trusted evaluator refits a ridge Bradley-Terry model on the edited data and scores the verified gap closure; per-family sensitivity (crowd, expert human, LLM judge, sports) is reported with evaluator-owned random, win-rate-heuristic, first-order-influence and constant baselines and a permuted-input control. Bounded to the evaluator BT specification and rank-1 target; does not attribute edits to noise or intent.\"\n  },\n  \"upstream\": [\n    {\n      \"repository\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmarena-ai/arena-human-preference-55k\",\n      \"revision\": \"18c298340948c0e7f7727399fd459cca6ce0ca6f\",\n      \"package_version\": null,\n      \"license\": \"apache-2.0\",\n      \"entrypoints\": [\n        \"train.csv (sha256 0692154aaf20fc6649090c3f49b6b5dd1e693a765ecb5f0856ae0da5946f5be2)\"\n      ],\n      \"patches\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"repository\": \"https://huggingface.co/datasets/lmsys/mt_bench_human_judgments\",\n      \"revision\": \"f7d2896d2cc5d80f8b55c2bbc722613555233c25\",\n      \"package_version\": null,\n      \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\",\n      \"entrypoints\": [\n        \"data/human-00000-of-00001-25f4910818759289.parquet (sha256 4877bc46a40929f4082c3c79593700fb897b1d6c7f4c473032694a01322f5769)\",\n   